{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '6415,6485p' 'Pickaxe-Puddles-Pick-Axe-Pete-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-031259/vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js' && sed -n '465,500p' 'Pickaxe-Puddles-Pick-Axe-Pete-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-031259/vendor/engine/API-INDEX.md'\"","aggregated_output":"    if (!b.onGround && wasGround && (b.vz || 0) <= 0 && !b.climbing) { const sz = this._surfaceBelow(b, Math.max(b.w / 2 + 3, Math.abs(b.vx || 0) * dt * 1.5 + 2)); if (sz !== null) { b.z = sz; b.vz = 0; b.onGround = true; } }\n    return b;\n  }\n  _stands(k, cx, cz, prevZ, top, b) {\n    if (k === 'solid') return true;\n    if (b.drop > 0 || prevZ < top - .01) return false;\n    if (k === 'oneway') return true;\n    return k === 'ladder' && !b.climbing && this.kind(cx, cz + 1) !== 'ladder';   // stand on the top of a ladder\n  }\n  _mx(b, dx, solids) {\n    const T = this.T, hw = b.w / 2; b.x += dx;\n    const cx = Math.floor((dx > 0 ? b.x + hw : b.x - hw) / T);\n    const blocked = () => { for (let cz = Math.floor((b.z + .01) / T); cz <= Math.floor((b.z + b.h - .01) / T); cz++) if (this.kind(cx, cz) === 'solid') return cz; return null; };\n    let hit = blocked();\n    if (hit !== null && b._grounded) {   // step up onto a low ledge (the top of a slope, a small step)\n      const top = (hit + 1) * T, up = top - b.z;\n      if (up > 0 && up <= (b.stepUp === undefined ? 5 : b.stepUp)) { const oz = b.z; b.z = top; if (blocked() === null) hit = null; else b.z = oz; }\n    }\n    if (hit !== null) { b.x = dx > 0 ? cx * T - hw - .001 : (cx + 1) * T + hw + .001; b.vx = 0; b.hitWall = dx > 0 ? 1 : -1; return true; }\n    if (solids) for (const s of solids) {\n      if (s.oneway || s.solid === false || s === b) continue;\n      if (Math.abs(b.x - s.x) * 2 < b.w + s.w && b.z < s.z + s.h - .01 && s.z < b.z + b.h - .01) { b.x = dx > 0 ? s.x - (s.w + b.w) / 2 - .001 : s.x + (s.w + b.w) / 2 + .001; b.vx = s.vx || 0; b.hitWall = dx > 0 ? 1 : -1; return true; }\n    }\n    return false;\n  }\n  _mz(b, dz, solids) {\n    const T = this.T, prev = b.z; b.z += dz;\n    const hw = b.w / 2 - .01, c0 = Math.floor((b.x - hw) / T), c1 = Math.floor((b.x + hw) / T);\n    if (dz <= 0) {\n      const cz = Math.floor(b.z / T), top = (cz + 1) * T, sc = Math.floor(b.x / T);\n      // slopes first: they hold the body at their surface under its center (check the row of the feet and the one above)\n      for (const rz of [cz + 1, cz]) if (this.kind(sc, rz) === 'slope') {\n        const sz = this.slopeZ(sc, rz, b.x);\n        if (b.z <= sz && prev >= sz - T * .5) { b.z = sz; if (b.vz < 0) b.vz = 0; b.onGround = true; b.onOneWay = false; return true; }\n      }\n      let land = false, one = true;\n      for (let cx = c0; cx <= c1; cx++) { const k = this.kind(cx, cz); if (k && this._stands(k, cx, cz, prev, top, b)) { land = true; if (k === 'solid') one = false; } }\n      if (land) { b.z = top; if (b.vz < 0) b.vz = 0; b.onGround = true; b.onOneWay = one; return true; }\n      if (solids) for (const s of solids) {\n        if (s.solid === false || s === b) continue; const st = s.z + s.h;\n        if (Math.abs(b.x - s.x) * 2 < b.w + s.w && b.z <= st && prev >= st - .01 - Math.max(0, -(s.vz || 0)) * .05 && !(s.oneway && b.drop > 0)) { b.z = st; if (b.vz < 0) b.vz = 0; b.onGround = true; b.onOneWay = !!s.oneway; b.ground = s; return true; }\n      }\n    } else {\n      const head = b.z + b.h, cz = Math.floor(head / T);\n      let best = null;\n      for (let cx = c0; cx <= c1; cx++) if (this.kind(cx, cz) === 'solid') { const d = Math.abs((cx + .5) * T - b.x); if (!best || d < best.d) best = { cx, cz, id: this.cell(cx, cz), d }; }\n      if (best) { b.z = cz * T - b.h - .001; b.vz = 0; b.hitCeiling = true; b.bumped = { cx: best.cx, cz: best.cz, id: best.id }; return true; }\n      if (solids) for (const s of solids) {\n        if (s.oneway || s.solid === false || s === b) continue;\n        if (Math.abs(b.x - s.x) * 2 < b.w + s.w && head > s.z && prev + b.h <= s.z + .01) { b.z = s.z - b.h - .001; b.vz = 0; b.hitCeiling = true; return true; }\n      }\n    }\n    return false;\n  }\n  /** standing still exactly on a surface: detect it without needing gravity */\n  _probe(b, solids) {\n    const T = this.T, hw = b.w / 2 - .01, cz = Math.floor((b.z - .25) / T), top = (cz + 1) * T;\n    const sc = Math.floor(b.x / T), zc = Math.floor((b.z - .01) / T);\n    if (this.kind(sc, zc) === 'slope' && Math.abs(b.z - this.slopeZ(sc, zc, b.x)) < .5) { b.onGround = true; b.onOneWay = false; return; }\n    if (Math.abs(b.z - top) < .3) for (let cx = Math.floor((b.x - hw) / T); cx <= Math.floor((b.x + hw) / T); cx++) { const k = this.kind(cx, cz); if (k && this._stands(k, cx, cz, b.z, top, b)) { b.onGround = true; b.onOneWay = k !== 'solid'; return; } }\n    if (solids) for (const s of solids) if (s.solid !== false && s !== b && Math.abs(b.x - s.x) * 2 < b.w + s.w && Math.abs(b.z - (s.z + s.h)) < .3) { b.onGround = true; b.ground = s; b.onOneWay = !!s.oneway; return; }\n  }\n  /** projected pixel bounds of the level for this view (use for game.cam.bounds) */\n  bounds(view) {\n    const W = this.w * this.T, H = this.h * this.T, d = this.depth / 2; let x0 = 1e9, y0 = 1e9, x1 = -1e9, y1 = -1e9;\n    for (const x of [0, W]) for (const y of [-d, d]) for (const z of [0, H]) { const s = view.p(x, y, z); x0 = Math.min(x0, s[0]); x1 = Math.max(x1, s[0]); y0 = Math.min(y0, s[1]); y1 = Math.max(y1, s[1]); }\n    return { x0, y0: y0 - 4, x1, y1: y1 + 4 };\n  }\n  /** start a crumbling block at a cell going, once (it falls away after holds seconds and comes back after respawn more;\n   *  0: never; update(dt) runs them, each step); returns its record */\n  crumble(cx, cz, holds = .5, respawn = 3) {\n- `new E.Game({ loop })`: false makes a game in a page that runs only by advance()\n- `new E.Game({ menu })`: the pause, settings and controls screens ({ items, settings, controls, quit } adjusts them, false leaves them out)\n- `new E.Game({ fullscreen })`: 'tap' (a phone goes full screen at its first tap and when a game starts, unless the player turned it off), 'button' (only when asked) or false\n- `new E.Game({ corner, backGesture })`: corner: the menu and full-screen buttons (top right); backGesture: a phone's back steps back in the game first (false: it leaves the page)\n- `new E.Game({ autoPause })`: a pausable scene pauses when the page is hidden or loses focus\n- `new E.Game({ live })`: true: a world that never stops for one player (online, a shared screen): a pause opens the menus over it, the scene's update goes on (game.paused says a menu is up) and the menu holds that player's input back\n- `new E.Game({ id })`: the name the player's settings are saved under (the page's path)\n- `new E.Game({ pace })`: false draws every refresh of a fast display even when the frames can't keep up (by default it draws every other one, evenly), unless the player picks Frame rate 60\n- `new E.Game({ camera })`: the camera of every scene without its own (a scene's camera option: the player's zoom, start)\n- `game.H`: the screen's height in game pixels (W is its width)\n- `game.W`: internal buffer size in pixels (HUD layout)\n- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n- `game.advance(seconds = this.o.step, o = {})`: run the game for `seconds` of real time in exact fixed steps, at once, without requestAnimationFrame: tests, tools and headless runs (advance(1) is 120 updates). o.draw: then draw one frame (not in a headless game). A headless game made with draw: true draws one frame each advance, on a stand-in renderer, so a draw error lands in game.errors (a test that catches what a player would see break). Returns the updates run\n- `game.after(seconds, fn, o = {})`: run fn once after `seconds` of game time. Cleared on scene change, unless { keep: true } (a site's clock, a watcher of the whole game: it outlives scenes, as a kept tween does). Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n- `game.back()`: a step back, as a phone's back gesture asks for (the engine calls it for one; a back button of the game's own can): the open menu screen goes back one; else the scene's own back() takes it (it returns true when it did); else a scene in play pauses into the menu, and a paused one goes on. Returns false where there is nowhere to go (a title)\n- `game.cornerArea()` †: where the corner's buttons (menu and full screen, top right; the touch START) cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (r.W and r.H's space), or null while none show: keep a HUD clear of it\n- `game.dispose()`: end the game for good: stop the loop and remove everything the engine added to the page (its listeners on the window, the document, the canvas and the buttons, the touch controls, the GPU lighting's canvas) and close the sound. Tests and tools that make many games call it; the canvas stays\n- `game.enableGPU(o = {})` †: turn on WebGPU lighting: where it can't draw (no WebGPU, a side view) the canvas lighting stands in, with its own ambient (game.lights.ambient) and the same lights. opts: { map, bands, ambient, fallback, ... }\n- `game.every(seconds, fn, o = {})`: run fn every `seconds` of game time. Cleared on scene change, unless { keep: true }. Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.fail(where, e)`: report an error in game code without stopping the game: logged once per place and message, kept in game.errors and shown on the error panel (the engine reports its own callbacks' errors this way): game.fail('power ' + id, err)\n- `game.flash(color = '#ffffff', seconds = .12, strength = 1)`: flash the whole screen with a color for `seconds` (dithered fade out): hits, explosions, lightning. Shorter when reduceMotion, dimmer by the player's settings.flashes\n- `game.focus(x, y, z = 0)`: camera follows this world point. Side-scrollers: game.focus(x, 0, z)\n- `game.follow(target, o = {})`: keep the camera on an object automatically (instead of calling focus every update). opts: { z: extra height to look at (default 16), lead: look ahead in the facing / moving direction }. follow(null) stops.\n- `game.freeze(s)`: hit-stop: the game stands still for s seconds (.04-.08 for a hit); input still ticks\n- `game.go(name, data, o = {})`: switch scene: game.go('play', { level: 2 }). It fades through black (dithered) unless opts.fade is 0 (a cut) or another number of seconds; opts.fade can name a transition instead: 'black', 'white', 'wipe', 'iris', 'mosaic', 'swirl' or 'dissolve', each way taking opts.seconds (.4), round opts.at (iris and swirl: a world point { x, y, z }, which each scene's camera places, or [x, y] on the screen; its centre by default). With reduce motion each is a plain fade\n- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', rumble: true })\n- `game.hook(kind, fn)` †: a function of the game's own on the engine's clock: kind 'input' fn(dt) every step, paused or not, after the input is read (a host's guard, an idle timer); 'step' fn(dt) every update step in play, before the scene's update (an attract mode's watcher); 'enter' fn(name, data) as a scene starts. Returns a function that removes it\n- `game.menu(name, o)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (menu: false, or the agent edition) it pauses a scene in play. o: { pause: false } opens it over a world that keeps stepping, as game.live does for every pause. Returns true when a menu opened\n- `game.mouseGround()`: the mouse's point on the ground: [x, y] in world units (an array, not { x, y }), or null with no mouse over the canvas\n- `game.nextView(dir = 1)`: cycle through game.views (or every view): bind it to a key for players who like to switch\n- `game.note(text, seconds = 1.2)`, `game.shownNote`: a short notice at the top of the screen (zoom level, saved, ...): game.note('ZOOM 1.5x', 1). game.shownNote is the one showing, { text, end } (end in game.real seconds), or null: a game that draws it its own way takes it and sets shownNote to null\n- `game.onView(f)` †: call f(view) whenever the view changes (re-bake caches, move HUD)\n- `game.pause(reason = 'player')`: pause the game, saying why ('player' | 'focus' | 'controller' | 'menu': pauseReason); returns true if it paused. The player resumes (Escape, Start, Resume); resume() does it from code\n- `game.players` †: the players: [game.input (player 1), ...the ones who joined (game.allowJoin, game.addPlayer: section 10j)]; each an input with player (1..4), name ('P1'), color (E.PLAYER_COLORS) and device. A game of one: [game.input]\n- `game.removePlayer(p)` †: a player leaves (its input, or its number, 2 to 4); player 1 has the whole keyboard back when no one shares it\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
