{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"tail -20 'Pickaxe-Puddles-Pick-Axe-Pete-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-031259/tests/audio-browser.py' && tail -25 'Pickaxe-Puddles-Pick-Axe-Pete-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-031259/tests/browser.py' && cat 'Pickaxe-Puddles-Pick-Axe-Pete-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-031259/docs/research.md'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"tail -20 'Pickaxe-Puddles-Pick-Axe-Pete-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-031259/tests/audio-browser.py' && tail -25 'Pickaxe-Puddles-Pick-Axe-Pete-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-031259/tests/browser.py' && cat 'Pickaxe-Puddles-Pick-Axe-Pete-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-031259/docs/research.md'\"","aggregated_output":"            const rescue=testInput.contextTarget.kind;\n            sim.miners[1].downed=false;testInput.update(1/120);\n            const door=testInput.contextTarget.kind;\n            sim.room.doors=[];testInput.update(1/120);\n            const redirect=testInput.contextTarget.kind;\n            return {rescue,door,redirect};\n        }\"\"\")\n        check(priorities=={\"rescue\":\"rescue\",\"door\":\"door\",\"redirect\":\"redirect\"},\"touch context rescue-door-redirect order\",priorities)\n        touch_page.evaluate(\"testInput.dispose();testGame.dispose()\")\n        touch_context.close()\n        browser.close()\n    for passed, name, detail in CHECKS:\n        if not passed:\n            print(f\"FAIL {name}: {json.dumps(detail)}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    print(f\"{sum(x[0] for x in CHECKS)}/{len(CHECKS)} audio/input checks passed\")\n    return all(x[0] for x in CHECKS)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(0 if run() else 1)\n    with sync_playwright() as p:\n        browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=True, args=[\"--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required\"])\n        for name, callback in [\n            (\"keyboard\", lambda: keyboard_checks(browser)),\n            (\"attract\", lambda: attract_checks(browser)),\n            (\"pad\", lambda: pad_checks(browser)),\n            (\"persistent controls\", lambda: persistence_checks(browser)),\n            (\"local co-op\", lambda: coop_checks(browser)),\n            (\"touch portrait\", lambda: touch_checks(browser, 390, 844)),\n            (\"touch landscape\", lambda: touch_checks(browser, 844, 390)),\n        ]:\n            try:\n                callback()\n            except Exception as exc:\n                check(False, name + \" scenario completed\", str(exc))\n        browser.close()\n    check(not CONSOLE, \"packaged browser has no console/page errors\", CONSOLE)\n    for failure in FAILURES:\n        print(\"FAIL \" + failure, file=sys.stderr)\n    print(f\"{sum(passed for passed, _ in CHECKS)}/{len(CHECKS)} integrated browser checks passed\")\n    return not FAILURES\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(0 if run() else 1)\n# Source research\n\nConsulted during this build on 2026-11-06. The game is an original adaptation of **Pick Axe Pete! (1982)** for the Odyssey².\n\n| Primary source | Confirmed facts |\n| --- | --- |\n| [US manual transcription](https://odyssey2.info/library/manuals/us_pickaxepete/pick-axe-pete.txt), saved as `source-manual.txt` | Three rock-emitting doors; temporary ladders and floor gaps; breakable picks; jumping and ducking; collision-produced tools; fleeting keys; keyless-door jams; pressure rises with gold and eases after a doorway. Relative awards are evade 1, strike 3, pick 5, key 10, door 20. Original multiplayer uses successive turns. |\n| [Videogaming Illustrated, October 1982, pp. 27–28](https://www.ataricompendium.com/archives/magazines/vg_ill/videogaming_ill_oct82.pdf#page=1) | Boulders roll and bounce; collision resources favor lower picks and upper keys; ladders retract; mines use seven shafts. Direct URL initially returned 404 through the browser fetch; the indexed PDF subsequently opened and its review text was inspected. |\n| [Archived mine screenshot](https://www.odyssey2.info/i/screens/pick-scr.gif), saved as `source-mine.gif` | Inspected locally: black field, red horizontal ledges with gaps, white ladder, contrasting cyan/white/magenta doors, blue rocks and a gold miner with pink pick. |\n| [Engine handoff/API card](https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691/dist/handoff) | Native code-drawn pixel art, posed 3D humanoids, fixed-tick Platformer/PlatformMap systems, side-view x/z gameplay plane. Vendored documentation is the implementation reference. |\n| [AI Hub Session Protocol v1](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869/lib/hub/README.md) | Host-authoritative shared world, zero-based player IDs, hidden nonplayer authority, readiness/countdown/results lifecycle, at most 20 outgoing game messages/s and 16 KB/message. |\n\n## Adaptations and unknowns\n\nDeliberate high/low ricochets, successful-contact tool wear, three health marks, shared-world co-op and rescue, seeded supply guarantees, checkpoint retries and a three-wave extraction are new design choices. New score and voice synthesis do not claim historical accuracy. The source game's exact sound synthesis, music and voice are **unknown** from the inspected material. No original audio is copied.\n\nThe dark whole-room composition, opposing resource chases, boulder pressure and doorway relief informed the new mine. Timber, work lights, mineral seams, original miner rigs and animated machinery expand that visual vocabulary using the supplied engine's native procedural style.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('exit-interview.json'); f=json.loads(p.read_text())\nf['testingFeedback']=[\n'18 unique defects were found across automated tests, visual checks and contract/state review; all were fixed. Repeated assertions of one cause are counted once.',\n'Four were critical: lost native movement state on restore, duplicate authoritative event IDs on restore, cropped phone control view, and incorrect Hub deadline/instruction metadata.',\n'Normal-input full expeditions on every route, including packet-loss and hidden-authority co-op, combined with deterministic mid-jump/mid-ladder snapshot continuation.',\n'Syntax-only checks: useful for packaging, but unable to establish movement, progression, networking or presentation.'\n]\nf['engineFeedback']=[\n'Native Platformer traversal and posed Humanoid rigs supplied responsive movement and readable continuous animation, with useful native shape, weapon and hat hooks.',\n'Yes. Map rows are top-first but cells are bottom-first; Platformer construction resets private movement timers; fixed-resolution screen scaling initially cropped narrow viewports.',\n'The deterministic supply director, rock collisions, tool/key economy, extraction encounters and authoritative Hub shared-world adapter.',\n'Keeping ladder topology, one-way floor contacts, animation and serialized native movement consistent across a renderer-free authority and visible clients.',\n'Patched Screen.resize to permit fractional scaling when the viewport is smaller than the logical buffer. Game adapters also preserve native movement internals and ladder-crossing one-way ledges; the pristine engine baseline remains vendored.',\n'Add native Platformer snapshot/restore with private movement timers, plus a fixed-resolution small-viewport regression case.'\n]\nf['promptFeedback']=[\n'The director plan specifies the complete action/resource loop, failure paths, accessibility and concrete proof to deliver.',\n'Standalone internet play versus Hub integration was ambiguous. Followed the plan: standalone solo/local co-op, and online shared-world co-op through AI Hub.',\n'Integrating one deterministic expedition across keyboard, pad, multitouch assists, attract play, couch ownership and a hidden online authority.',\n'Use a shorter prioritized acceptance list and distinguish desired pacing from hard functional gates. Skilled scripted runs here take roughly two minutes; a ten-to-twelve-minute first success was not measured.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(f,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('exit-interview.json'); f=json.loads(p.read_text())\nf['testingFeedback']=[\n'18 unique defects were found across automated tests, visual checks and contract/state review; all were fixed. Repeated assertions of one cause are counted once.',\n'Four were critical: lost native movement state on restore, duplicate authoritative event IDs on restore, cropped phone control view, and incorrect Hub deadline/instruction metadata.',\n'Normal-input full expeditions on every route, including packet-loss and hidden-authority co-op, combined with deterministic mid-jump/mid-ladder snapshot continuation.',\n'Syntax-only checks: useful for packaging, but unable to establish movement, progression, networking or presentation.'\n]\nf['engineFeedback']=[\n'Native Platformer traversal and posed Humanoid rigs supplied responsive movement and readable continuous animation, with useful native shape, weapon and hat hooks.',\n'Yes. Map rows are top-first but cells are bottom-first; Platformer construction resets private movement timers; fixed-resolution screen scaling initially cropped narrow viewports.',\n'The deterministic supply director, rock collisions, tool/key economy, extraction encounters and authoritative Hub shared-world adapter.',\n'Keeping ladder topology, one-way floor contacts, animation and serialized native movement consistent across a renderer-free authority and visible clients.',\n'Patched Screen.resize to permit fractional scaling when the viewport is smaller than the logical buffer. Game adapters also preserve native movement internals and ladder-crossing one-way ledges; the pristine engine baseline remains vendored.',\n'Add native Platformer snapshot/restore with private movement timers, plus a fixed-resolution small-viewport regression case.'\n]\nf['promptFeedback']=[\n'The director plan specifies the complete action/resource loop, failure paths, accessibility and concrete proof to deliver.',\n'Standalone internet play versus Hub integration was ambiguous. Followed the plan: standalone solo/local co-op, and online shared-world co-op through AI Hub.',\n'Integrating one deterministic expedition across keyboard, pad, multitouch assists, attract play, couch ownership and a hidden online authority.',\n'Use a shorter prioritized acceptance list and distinguish desired pacing from hard functional gates. Skilled scripted runs here take roughly two minutes; a ten-to-twelve-minute first success was not measured.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(f,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
