{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nroot=Path('.')\np=root/'exit-interview.json';f=json.loads(p.read_text())\nf['testingFeedback'][0]='24 unique defects were found across automated tests, visual checks and contract/state review; all were fixed. Repeated assertions of one cause are counted once.'\np.write_text(json.dumps(f,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\ndev=root/\\\"Pickaxe-Puddles-Pick-Axe-Pete-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-031259\\\"\np=dev/'docs/testing.md';s=p.read_text().replace('following18distinct','following24distinct').replace('The following18distinct','The following24distinct')\ns=s.replace('SUN/MOON/STAR in113.02/123.08/125.50simulation seconds','SUN/MOON/STAR in139.99/121.20/182.67simulation seconds')\ns=s.replace('in118.8/120.37/124.76s; hidden nonplayer authority completes in127.46s','in a little over two simulation minutes on the recorded seeded routes; hidden nonplayer authority also completes with substantial margin')\ns=s.replace('the following18distinct','the following24distinct')\ns=s.replace('| D18 | Minor | Attract reset review | Cosmetic clock/camera state survived a fresh view reset. Clear those presentation fields at new-run boundaries. |','| D18 | Minor | Attract reset review | Cosmetic clock/camera state survived fresh resets, while old event history could replay across chambers. Clear presentation fields only at new-run boundaries and retain seen IDs across chamber changes. |\\\\n| D19 | Minor | Actual local co-op browser test | A pad transferred from player one to a joining player two looked like a disconnect and spuriously paused. Ignore that native lost-pad signal when another local seat now owns the pad; retain true unplug pauses. |\\\\n| D20 | Minor | Controller audit + native test | Circle/B had menu-back semantics but no off-menu duck mapping. Map it contextually to duck without changing menu navigation or ladder control. |\\\\n| D21 | Major | Content audit + route tests | Door routes initially changed speed and seam positions but lacked distinct authored layouts/ore profiles. Added original/mirrored/staggered gaps, route palettes, ore weightings and actual route bonuses. |\\\\n| D22 | Major | Expanded normal-input route tests | The pilot released Jump one tick after takeoff and cut evasive jumps. Sustain Jump during ascent and prioritize a falling pick while unarmed. Human jump physics already worked. |\\\\n| D23 | Major | Mouse audit + actual browser hold | Clicking a rescue marker sent only a one-tick action. Retain a range-checked mouse target and held Interact until release, consuming the overlapping chop. |\\\\n| D24 | Major | Rule audit + collision regression | Unredirected ore collisions could destroy reinforced heavy rocks. Heavy ore now survives drifting collisions and shatters through three chops or a deliberately redirected collision. |')\ns=s.replace('- Screenshots in','- tests/webkit.py: independent WebKit file launch, uncropped phone geometry, real touch jump, pause/settings and native error checks in portrait and landscape.\\\\n- Screenshots in')\np.write_text(s)\np=dev/'docs/testing-sim.md';s=p.read_text().replace('28 substantive cases','29 substantive cases').replace('139.99 s (SUN, score 316, 1 helmet)','139.99 s (SUN, score 298, 1 helmet)').replace('178.00 s (STAR, score 348, 3 helmets)','182.67 s (STAR, score 463, 3 helmets)').replace('three-contact heavy ore;','three-contact heavy ore; reinforced ore surviving unredirected collisions;');p.write_text(s)\np=dev/'docs/authoring.md';s=p.read_text().replace('SUN/MOON/STAR speed profiles and change the next chamber’s arrangement, palette and risk.','SUN/MOON/STAR speed profiles, original/mirrored/staggered gaps, distinct ore-weight profiles and warm/cool/coral work lights. MOON gold pickups award5; STAR collision bonuses add3.');p.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
